---
// Shared honest-expectations block, verbatim copy per the late-2026 campaign spec.
---

<section class="py-14 md:py-20 bg-white">
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto reveal">
      <p class="lt26-eyebrow lt26-eyebrow--light">What you still do</p>
      <div class="lt26-divider"></div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-6">The honest part</h2>
      <p class="mt-6 text-base md:text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
        You'll get a trained person, and you'll still need to train them on how your firm does things. We handle sourcing, vetting, baseline legal-support training, QA, coaching, and performance management. You onboard them like any new hire, embed them in your systems, and invest real time in the first 30 to 60 days.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base md:text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
        What you skip is the recruiting cycle and the turnover risk, not the onboarding. Firms that treat this like welcoming a new employee win.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
